sentences.text:
The anticipatory bail application is opposed by the learned AGA bringing before this Court following facts and circumstances:-
(i) The applicant is named in the FIR imputing direct allegations against him;
(ii) There is no evidence to show that she died in the hospital, in fact the inquest was done in their own house;
(iii) The deceased, just before her death, complained to her brother as to the fact of not providing medical assistance which she needed the most and because of extreme carelessness and disinterest shown by them in the background of demand of dowry and in the background of allegations of torture and harassment, the death has been caused.

Therefore, it is argued that the case definitely comes within the definition of Section 304-B IPC;
(iv) Mere presence of a clinical tape cannot be taken as an evidence of medical treatment at the hospital, further no medical papers have been filed on behalf of the applicant to show that she was being properly taken care of by providing timely medical help;
(v) It is also pointed out that against rest of the two accused persons namely,
Yashveer and Satyavati charge sheet has been filed and investigation is pending against the present applicant because he was not available for interrogation.
